;; spec:   stdlib §5.5 S2, §2.11, §7 L21 (callable collections)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 30
;; audit:  clean
;; open:   L21
;; Clojure's (m k) and (v i): a Map is a function of its key, returning an
;; Option (the `get` it eta-expands to), a Vec a function of its index.
;; Today only a function is callable: `cannot unify (Map i64 i64) with (fn
;; (a) b)` and `cannot unify (Vec i64) with (fn (a) b)` (A11 t51, k2).
;; This case is the collections half of S2 (tranche 3); the keyword half, `(:k x)`,
;; is tranche 2's and is case 1000 (`open:` L14), split off from this one by Z0.
(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((m (assoc (map-empty) 1 10))
        (v [5 20 7]))
    (+ (match (m 1) ((some x) x) (nil 0)) (v 1))))
